msgid "What&#8217;s new?"
msgstr ""

msgid "We just released Quarkus 0.19.1."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This new version brings a lot of new extensions, especially in the "
"persistence area."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Quarkus 0.19.1 is still targeting GraalVM 19.0.2 as we discovered a bug in "
"GraalVM 19.1.0 that affects Quarkus."
msgstr ""

msgid "The issue is already fixed but we are waiting for a 19.1.1 release."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Here are the main highlights of this release: MongoDB support, Neo4J "
"support, Amazon DynamoDB support, Apache Tika support, Reactive Messaging "
"MQTT support and better Hibernate ORM schema upgrade (useful for dev mode)."
msgstr ""

msgid "Hibernate ORM schema management improvements"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"We had a few issues with automatic schema upgrades handled by Hibernate ORM. "
"Things are now smoother and we significantly improved the documentation to "
"explain https://quarkus.io/guides/hibernate-orm#hibernate-orm-in-development-"
"mode[how to configure schema management in various situations]."
msgstr ""

msgid "New extensions"
msgstr ""

msgid "MongoDB extension"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"https://www.mongodb.com/[MongoDB] needs no introduction as it's probably the "
"most widely used NoSQL datastore.\n"
"We had a lot of users asking for MongoDB support in Quarkus and here we are: "
"we now have a fully featured MongoDB client extension."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"It supports imperative and reactive and comes with a lot of configuration "
"properties to tune the client. And, of course, you can use it with GraalVM."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You can learn more about it in the link:/guides/mongodb[MongoDB client "
"guide]."
msgstr ""

msgid "Neo4j extension"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"https://neo4j.com/[Neo4j] is a graph database management system focused not "
"only on the data itself, but especially on the relations between data."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Neo4j offers Cypher, a declarative query language much like SQL.\n"
"Cypher is used to query the graph, telling the database engine what patterns "
"to match and how.\n"
"Clients communicate over the so called Bolt protocol with the database."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Quarkus now offers a Neo4j extension so that you can easily use Neo4j with "
"Quarkus in JVM and native mode."
msgstr ""

msgid "Want to give it a try? We have link:/guides/neo4j[a guide] for you."
msgstr ""

msgid "Amazon DynamoDB extension"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"https://aws.amazon.com/dynamodb/[Amazon DynamoDB] is a key-value and "
"document database available on AWS."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The first version of this extensions allow to leverage Amazon DynamoDB "
"features in JVM and native mode but it is not fully \"quarked\" yet.\n"
"Future iterations will bring Quarkus-style config and the ability to inject "
"the client directly with CDI."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"In the meantime, you can create your client manually and give us feedback "
"about the configuration knobs you want us to expose."
msgstr ""

msgid "Apache Tika extension"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"http://tika.apache.org/[Apache Tika] is a framework to extract data from "
"documents (and especially binary ones such as PDF documents). With the "
"Apache Tika Quarkus extension, just inject a `TikaParser` and you can "
"extract the information from your documents. Yes, in native mode too."
msgstr ""

msgid "Reactive Messaging MQTT connector"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"http://mqtt.org/[MQTT] is a machine-to-machine/IoT connectivity protocol. "
"Our reactive messaging layer is growing and we now have support for it."
msgstr ""

msgid "Full changelog"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"We also fixed some issues and merged a lot of improvements all over the "
"place."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"You can find https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/releases/tag/0.19.0[the "
"full changelog of 0.19.0 release on GitHub] and also https://github.com/"
"quarkusio/quarkus/releases/tag/0.19.1[the additional issues we fixed in 0.19."
"1]."
msgstr ""

msgid "Where is 0.19.0?"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"We found a regression in our Gradle support while releasing 0.19.0, that's "
"why we released 0.19.1 right away."
msgstr ""

msgid "Contributors"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Quarkus has now https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/graphs/contributors[116 "
"contributors].\n"
"Many many thanks to each and everyone of them."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"In particular for this release, thanks to Alessio Soldano, Alexey "
"Loubyansky, Arnost Valicek, Clement Escoffier, David M. Lloyd, Emmanuel "
"Bernard, Federico Fissore, Gary Tierney, George Gastaldi, Georgios "
"Andrianakis, Guillaume Dufour, Guillaume Smet, Gwenneg Lepage, Jason T. "
"Greene, Jasper Huzen, Ken Finnigan, Loïc Mathieu, Maciej Swiderski, Manyanda "
"Chitimbo, Marcin Czeczko, Martin Kouba, Martin Panzer, Martin Stefanko, "
"Michael Simons, Michal Szynkiewicz, Pedro Igor, Romain Quinio, Rostislav "
"Svoboda, Sanne Grinovero, Sergey Beryozkin, Stéphane Epardaud and Stuart "
"Douglas."
msgstr ""

msgid "Come Join Us"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"We value your feedback a lot so please report bugs, ask for improvements... "
"Let's build something great together!"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If you are a Quarkus user or just curious, don't be shy and join our "
"welcoming community:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"provide feedback on https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/issues[GitHub];"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"craft some code and https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/pulls[push a PR];"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"discuss with us on https://quarkusio.zulipchat.com/[Zulip] and on the https:/"
"/groups.google.com/d/forum/quarkus-dev[mailing list];"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"ask your questions on https://stackoverflow.com/questions/tagged/"
"quarkus[Stack Overflow]."
msgstr ""
